  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Karl Pearson's coefficient"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "$r = Cov(x, y)/(\\sigma_x\\sigma_y)$, where $Cov(x, y) = \\sum (x - \\bar{x})(y - \\bar{y})/n$. Equivalently $r = \\sum dx\\,dy / \\sqrt{\\sum dx^2 \\sum dy^2}$ with deviations from the means. r = +1 is perfect positive, −1 perfect negative, 0 no linear correlation.",
    "kn": "r = Cov(x, y)/(σₓσᵧ); Cov(x, y) = Σ(x − x̄)(y − ȳ)/n. r = Σdx·dy/√(Σdx²·Σdy²). r = +1 ಪರಿಪೂರ್ಣ ಧನ, −1 ಪರಿಪೂರ್ಣ ಋಣ, 0 ರೇಖೀಯ ಸಹಸಂಬಂಧ ಇಲ್ಲ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "−1 ≤ r ≤ 1"
    },
    {
     "en": "r has no units"
    },
    {
     "en": "Unaffected by change of origin and scale"
    }
   ],
   "formula": "r = \\frac{\\sum (x-\\bar{x})(y-\\bar{y})}{\\sqrt{\\sum (x-\\bar{x})^2 \\sum (y-\\bar{y})^2}}",
   "narration": {
    "en": "r = Cov(x, y)/(\\sigma_x\\sigma_y), where Cov(x, y) = \\sum (x - \\bar{x})(y - \\bar{y})/n. Equivalently r = \\sum dx\\,dy / \\sqrt{\\sum dx^2 \\sum dy^2} with deviations from the means. r = +1 is perfect positive, −1 perfect negative, 0 no linear correlation.",
    "kn": "r = Cov(x, y)/(σₓσᵧ); Cov(x, y) = Σ(x − x̄)(y − ȳ)/n. r = Σdx·dy/√(Σdx²·Σdy²). r = +1 ಪರಿಪೂರ್ಣ ಧನ, −1 ಪರಿಪೂರ್ಣ ಋಣ, 0 ರೇಖೀಯ ಸಹಸಂಬಂಧ ಇಲ್ಲ."
   }
  },
